    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "At first glance, Daisy Harris may seem like your grandmother. She loves birds (there’s one outside her window right now). She has a cat named Fluffy. She enjoys "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "knitting",
            "ref": "v-knit"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and likes talking about it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But dig a little deeper, and you’ll find that Daisy is not an old lady at all. She is a conversational AI chatbot created by British "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "telecommunications",
            "zh": "电信"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " company O2 to help fight "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "fraud",
            "zh": "诈骗"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Her mission, according to O2, is to “keep fraudsters on the line and waste as much of their time as possible”. This way, real people are protected from fraud."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Daisy’s tricks have kept many fraudsters on the line for 40 minutes at a time. In one call recording O2 released, a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "scammer",
            "zh": "诈骗分子"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " tries to get Daisy to download an app. She replies, “Dear, did you say pastry? I’m not quite sure what page I’m on.” She then complains that her screen has gone blank, saying, “It’s as black as the night sky.” When she finally tries to find the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "icon",
            "ref": "v-icon"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the scammer wants her to click, she says, “I see a pastry-like icon, but I’m not sure if it’s the right one. You know, my eyesight isn’t what it used to be.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There are many human "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "scambaiters",
            "zh": "诈骗诱捕者"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " out there. These people try to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "spot",
            "ref": "v-spot"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " would-be scammers and talk to them to stop them from reaching their targets. But they can’t work around the clock or talk to thousands of scammers at once. “This is where AI can and should come in,” says Morten Legarth, who helped develop Daisy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Unlike human scambaiters, Daisy doesn’t need sleep. And she has “all the time in the world”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "While Daisy does help fight fraud, some think her value is limited. Elisabeth Carter, a British crime expert, points out that Daisy “can’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "rid",
            "ref": "v-rid"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the world of scammers”. Carter also advises people not to follow Daisy’s lead in fooling around with scammers. Although it may feel satisfying, “the best thing to do if you get a call from a fraudster is to hang up and report it,” she says."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
